<title>UK: BTG says to split shares to 10p each.</title>
<headline>BTG says to split shares to 10p each.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified group BTG Plc said on Monday that it would seek its shareholders' approval to split each of its 50p shares into five ordinary shares of 10 pence each.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the split was intended to improve the marketability of its shares.</p>
<p>The company called an extraordinary general meeting of its shareholders on December 18, 1996 and said the split would take effect from December 19.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171-542 7717</p>
</text>
